# A Dart package, not an application, so the lock file is not committed.
#
# `flutter pub get` resolves the same versions from the same constraints on every
# machine, and the lock file is 11 kB of noise in review. This is the standard
# split: applications lock, libraries do not.
#
# The APKs are the applications, and their lock files *are* committed. That is the
# distinction, not "which directory".
pubspec.lock